<h2 class="wp-block-heading">See it as a chart: the hour hides two rush hours</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A raw "hour" number treats 13:00 and 20:00 as just numbers. A histogram of order times shows two clear peaks, lunch and dinner, which is why features like <code>dinner</code> (19–22) help a model far more than the raw hour.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:code -->
<pre class="wp-block-code"><code class="language-python">import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
import numpy as np

rng = np.random.default_rng(11)
hours = np.concatenate([rng.normal(13, 1.0, 400), rng.normal(20.5, 1.2, 600), rng.uniform(8, 23, 200)])
